 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-- **Precision**: The comparison `nodes[i].size < min_size` relies on floating-point precision. If sizes are equal, the first node encountered is kept.
-- **Boundary Conditions**: If `nodes` contains null pointers or invalid indices, the code will crash. The source does not show null checks [S1, unofficial].
-- **Sign Extraction**: The bit shift `(corners >> c) & 1` assumes `corners` is an integer bitmask. If `corners` is stored differently, this logic fails [S1, unofficial].
-- **Flip Logic**: The `flip` variable is set based on `m1 != MATERIAL_AIR`. This determines the winding order of the output triangles. Incorrect flip logic leads to inverted normals [S1, unofficial].
